All done. Here's what was added:

**`txtar/archive.go`** — new method `Lookup`:
```go
// Lookup returns the file with the given name, or nil and false
// when the archive has no such file.
func (a *Archive) Lookup(name string) (*File, bool) {
	for i := range a.Files {
		if a.Files[i].Name == name {
			return &a.Files[i], true
		}
	}
	return nil, false
}
```
It iterates over `a.Files` by index so the returned pointer refers directly into the archive's slice (not a loop copy).

**`txtar/archive_test.go`** — new test `TestLookup` covering both the found and not-found cases.

All tests pass: `ok  golang.org/x/tools/txtar`

